FINAL ANSWER:
Bus factor: **2** for the project as a whole. Only **Troy Goode** is currently active on the core code. Douglas Christopher Wilson owns the most history but has been inactive since 2021-09-07.

Scope: 354 commits, 15 tracked files, history through 2026-04-12. The repo is small, so I read per-file history directly instead of sampling.

## Contributors

| Contributor | Commits (non-merge) | Last commit | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 143 | 2021-09-07 | Inactive (about 5 years) |
| Troy Goode | 95 | 2026-04-10 | Active |
| dependabot[bot] | 11 | 2026-03-02 | Bot |
| Everyone else | 1–4 each | n/a | Occasional |

Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson account for about 238 of the 354 commits. Nobody else has more than 4.

## Single-owner risk

| File | Top contributor | Share of commits | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` (the only source file, 238 lines) | Troy Goode | 29 of 62 (47%) | **High**. Everything depends on it, and the next-largest contributors have 4 commits each. |
| `test/vary.js` | Troy Goode | 1 of 1 | Medium |
| `test/issue-2.js` | Troy Goode | 10 of 12 (83%) | Medium |
| `test/example-app.js` | Troy Goode | 10 of 13 (77%) | Medium |
| `test/test.js` (731 lines, main suite) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 8 of 11 (73%) | **High**. The owner is inactive. |
| `package.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 68 of 113 (60%) | Medium. Troy Goode has 37 commits, so two people know it. |
| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 10 of 16 (63%) | Low. Ulises Gascón and Ignacio Mangas have also touched it. |
| `README.md` | Troy Goode | 29 of 66 (44%) | Low |
| `.eslintrc.yml`, `test/.eslintrc.yml`, `test/support/env.js` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 1 of 1 | Low (tiny config files) |
| `.github/dependabot.yml` | Ulises Gascón | 1 of 1 | Low |
| `.github/workflows/codeql.yml`, `scorecard.yml` | dependabot[bot] | 4 of 5 and 7 of 9 | Low. Updates are automated, and no person owns them. |

## Findings

- **Active code knowledge depends on Troy Goode.** In the last year they made 2 of the 4 non-bot commits that touched `lib/` or `test/`. The other two came from Fiona Formatter (a formatting-only commit) and Phillip Barta/Vansh Sharma/Jon Church-style one-off contributions, none of whom own any file.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson is a historical single point of knowledge.** They own `test/test.js`, most of `package.json` history and the CI setup. The history is still readable, but nobody active has deep context there.
- **`lib/index.js` has real contributors beyond these two.** Before the reformat commit, `git blame` shows Troy Goode 160 lines, Douglas Christopher Wilson 22, Alejandro Caravaca Puchades 12 and Raymond Feng 7. So the implementation is mostly Troy Goode's, with a thin tail of other authors.
- **Plain `git blame` is misleading right now.** The latest commit (`62628c0`, Fiona Formatter, a 4-space/double-quote reformat) shows 214 of 238 lines in `lib/index.js` as Fiona Formatter's. Ignore that attribution. To fix it, add the commit to `.git-blame-ignore-revs` and run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`.
- **Limits of this analysis.** I used commit counts and blame, not review activity, so people who reviewed code without committing are not counted. I did not run the import-dependents check, because the repo has one source file and everything depends on it. Contributor names may be split across aliases. For example, I saw "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades", "Alejandro García Fernández" and "Alejandro Oviedo", which may or may not be the same person. I did not merge them.

## Recommendations

1. Immediate: get a second active maintainer to review changes to `lib/index.js`. Troy Goode is the only current owner of the core code.
2. Short term: have someone active read through `test/test.js` and own it. It is the largest file and its main author is gone.
3. Ongoing: add `.git-blame-ignore-revs` for `62628c0` so ownership data stays usable. Document release and CI steps, because Douglas Christopher Wilson set up most of that and has left.

