**Bus factor: 2 for the whole repository.** Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together hold 72.5% of the surviving lines. The bus factor here is the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted. Reaching 80% takes 4 authors. Scope: all 18 files, 1,985 attributed lines, 315 non-merge commits.

**Whole repository, by surviving lines**

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses, merged) | 810 | 40.8% | 95 (30.2%) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | 31.7% | 143 (45.4%) |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | 4.8% | 2 |
| Jon Church | 72 | 3.6% | 3 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | 3.4% | 2 |

Troy Goode is one person only if the two addresses are the same person. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` holds 762 lines (38.4%) and `troy@laptop.example` holds 48 (2.4%). The merge is a guess from the shared name and addresses. Unmerged, the whole-repository bus factor is also 2 (70.1%, 80% needs 5 authors). I did not write a `.mailmap`, so nothing is permanently merged.

**Directories that depend on one person (bus factor 1)**

- **`lib/` (1 file, 238 lines): Troy Goode holds 66.8% (159 lines).** Douglas Christopher Wilson is next with 9.2%. This is the core code and the clearest single-person dependency.
- **`test/` (7 files, 966 lines): Troy Goode holds 53.5% (517 lines).** Douglas Christopher Wilson holds 38.7%.

**Directories with a bus factor of 2**

- **Root files (6 files, 415 lines):** Troy Goode (32.3%) and Douglas Christopher Wilson (27.7%) together hold 60.0%.
- **`.github/` (4 files, 366 lines):** Douglas Christopher Wilson (32.2%) and Íñigo Marquínez Prado (26.0%) together hold 58.2%. Nobody here holds half alone.

**What was left out**

- **Reformat commit:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter, 2026-04-12). It would otherwise give Fiona 291 lines (14.7%). Without the correction, the bus factor is still 2 (58.9%).
- **Bots:** 1 bot identity (10 lines, 11 commits) is excluded.
- **Unattributed lines:** 10 of 1,995 lines could not be attributed.
- **Generated or vendored files:** none were reported as dropped.

**Caveats**

- **Commit counts:** Douglas Christopher Wilson has the most commits (143, 45.4%). Troy Goode holds more of the code that is left.
- **What the numbers measure:** they show how concentrated the surviving code is, not who understands it. They don't show review work, design work or code that was deleted on purpose.
- **Small sample:** this is a small repository (1,985 lines), so a few commits can move these shares a lot.

**Recommendation:** have someone other than Troy Goode review and take over `lib/` and `test/`. If you confirm the two Troy Goode addresses are one person, I can write the `.mailmap` line so the merge applies to later runs.

